From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS / webOS Ports <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] terminal: make ch_ESC constexpr so it has a definition

  undefined reference to `Terminal::ch_ESC'

ch_ESC is an in-class initialised static const. Passing it to QChar() and
QString::arg() odr-uses it, which requires an out-of-class definition that
this code never provided; compilers previously folded the constant away and
hid the omission.

static constexpr members are implicitly inline since C++17, so this both
supplies the missing definition and keeps the constant foldable, without
adding a definition to terminal.cpp.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/terminal.h
+++ b/terminal.h
@@ -144,7 +144,7 @@
 
 private:
     Q_DISABLE_COPY(Terminal)
-    static const char ch_ESC = 0x1B; //escape
+    static constexpr char ch_ESC = 0x1B; //escape
     static const int maxScrollBackLines = 300;
 
     void insertAtCursor(QChar c, bool overwriteMode=true, bool advanceCursor=true);
